60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Looking at the options, a Flat Annual Fee seems the safest for the treasurer and the atmosphere, though it doesn't solve the newcomer barrier.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, I agree. A Flat Annual Fee is the only option that doesn't exponentially increase the administrative burden or risk the treasurer's sanity.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I'm still torn, but Tiered Membership might address the imbalance I found without the chaos of activity-based charging, provided it doesn't create the friction Takumi mentioned.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, the named-grade history Takumi found suggests tiers create a social divide. Activity-Based Charging is out because it kills turnout. I'm leaning toward the Flat Annual Fee for the sake of the atmosphere.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, the minute books were clear: tiers cause friction and make people withdraw. A Flat Annual Fee is the only way to ensure our fixed costs are covered without creating a social hierarchy or a bookkeeping nightmare.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, you're right about the friction, but we still have the issue of people refusing to join because of the upfront cost. Is there any way to make the Flat Annual Fee more flexible?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, we could potentially allow monthly installments, but that brings us back to the treasurer's workload. However, it's still far better than chasing a dozen small fees every single week.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, if we can manage installments without burning out the treasurer, then the Flat Annual Fee becomes much more palatable. It maintains the community feel while easing the entry barrier.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, exactly. If we keep the fee flat, we avoid the ""pay-to-play"" mentality that kills the weekday vibe. It's the only way to ensure people just show up without overthinking it.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, as long as we set the figure based on the actual fixed costs and not a guess, I'm on board. It's the most stable way to keep the lights on without causing a fight.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I'm satisfied that the Flat Annual Fee is the most balanced choice. It protects the atmosphere and the treasurer, and we can handle the newcomer issue through a few simple payment arrangements.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, I concur. The logic is sound: it minimizes administrative chaos and avoids the social friction of tiers. It is the most rational choice for the long-term health of the club.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I'll concede. While it doesn't perfectly solve the imbalance of use, it's clearly the only option that doesn't risk breaking the club's social fabric or its administration. I vote for the Flat Annual Fee.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I'm with you all. It preserves the sense of belonging and keeps the door open for everyone without the hesitation of a per-event charge. I vote for the Flat Annual Fee.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,It's the only option that guarantees our fixed costs are covered without bringing back the drama of the grade system. I vote for the Flat Annual Fee.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for the Flat Annual Fee. It is the most sustainable path for our community.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for the Flat Annual Fee. It is the most logical solution to our administrative and financial constraints.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,pass,Jonathan,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
